  "refutation_reason": "The objection fails because it treats a conditional capability ('enables... to meet') as an absolute guarantee for all implementations. The counterexample cites a specific scenario (consumer hardware) where the constraint is not met; however, this does not invalidate the assertion that systems exist or are enabled to meet these constraints under appropriate conditions. A failure in one specific implementation does not refute the general claim of enablement for meeting latency constraints. Therefore, the case does not successfully refute the literal graph assertion.",
